[center][size=6][color=#42FA60][b]House Rules[/b][/color][/size]
[b]Vanilla mechanics. Your rules.[/b]
[color=#A8B5A8]Available through Dear Modding UI or MCM[/color][/center]

[b]House Rules[/b] puts over 200 Fallout 4 settings in one menu. Keep Survival's needs but bring back manual saves. Adjust damage, slow down leveling, or make fusion cores last longer. Change the parts that don't suit your playthrough without installing a full overhaul.

No new gameplay systems, no ESP, and no plugin-slot cost. Survival unlocks are off by default.

[size=5][color=#42FA60][b]FEATURES[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Survival unlocks:[/b] Enable the console, manual saves, auto-saves, fast travel, and compass markers. Remove extra ammo or aid weight, allow god mode, re-enter Survival, and keep your exit save.[/*]
[*][b]Survival needs:[/b] Adjust hunger, thirst, sleep, diseases, and Adrenaline. Disable individual systems without leaving Survival difficulty.[/*]
[*][b]Healing and penalties:[/b] Change Stimpak healing and limb repair, RadAway strength, Rad-X potency, food healing, and the severity of hunger, thirst, and sleep penalties.[/*]
[*][b]Combat and difficulty:[/b] Set incoming and outgoing damage per difficulty, adjust armor formulas, VATS, perk chances, and legendary chance and rarity.[/*]
[*][b]Character and progression:[/b] Tune AP, sprint cost, carry weight, health, regeneration, XP, sneaking, pickpocketing, hacking, and lockpicking.[/*]
[*][b]Power armor:[/b] Adjust fusion core drain, jetpack use, and player or NPC armor durability.[/*]
[*][b]World settings:[/b] Change vendor prices, companion affinity gains and cooldowns, settler limits, and workshop build settings.[/*]
[/list]

For individual settings, defaults, and behavior notes, see the [url=https://github.com/northaxosky/fallout4-house-rules/blob/master/docs/FEATURES.md][b]full feature reference[/b][/url].

[size=5][color=#42FA60][b]CHOOSE YOUR MENU[/b][/color][/size]
One download, with a choice in the installer:
[list]
[*][b]Dear Modding UI:[/b] Native pages organized into Overview, Survival & Healing, Character & Progression, Combat, and World. Includes search, a modified-settings filter, and individual setting resets.[/*]
[*][b]MCM:[/b] The familiar Mod Configuration Menu interface, with the same gameplay settings.[/*]
[/list]

Both options use the same plugin and saved settings. The native option does not require MCM and does not install an extra MCM page, so House Rules won't appear twice in DMUI on a clean installation.

[size=5][color=#42FA60][b]REQUIREMENTS[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*]Fallout 4 on Windows[/*]
[*][url=https://f4se.silverlock.org/]F4SE[/url] matching your game version[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/47327]Address Library for F4SE Plugins[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://github.com/Dear-Modding-FO4/DearModdingUI]Dear Modding UI[/url] for the native menu, or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/21497]Mod Configuration Menu (MCM)[/url] for the MCM option[/*]
[/list]

Includes support for [b]1.10.163 (OG), 1.10.984 (NG), and 1.11.240 (AE)[/b].

[size=5][color=#42FA60][b]INSTALLATION & USAGE[/b][/color][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install F4SE, Address Library, and your preferred menu framework.[/*]
[*]Install House Rules through your mod manager. Choose [b]Dear Modding UI[/b] or [b]MCM[/b] in the FOMOD installer.[/*]
[*]Launch Fallout 4 through F4SE, using MO2 if that's how you manage your mods.[/*]
[*]Open House Rules in your chosen menu and adjust the settings you want.[/*]
[/list]

In [b]Dear Modding UI[/b], changes save when you finish editing a control. There's no Apply button. In [b]MCM[/b], close the pause menu to apply your changes.

[b]Saved settings:[/b] Data\MCM\Settings\HouseRules.ini
Both menu options read this file. The folder name is retained for MCM compatibility; native DMUI reads it directly.

[size=5][color=#42FA60][b]THINGS TO KNOW[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*]Consumable changes affect the next item you use, not an effect already running.[/*]
[*]The Survival carry-weight unlock needs a save reload to refresh effects already applied to your character or companions.[/*]
[*]Survival system toggles may wait for the manager script's next update. Reloading your save can refresh them sooner.[/*]
[*]If you change settings at the main menu or during loading, they are saved and applied once a save is ready.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Switching menus:[/b] Reinstall House Rules with the other option and restart the game. Use your mod manager's replace option rather than merging old files. Leftover MCM page files can cause a duplicate entry through DMUI's MCM bridge. Back up HouseRules.ini if your mod manager removes the whole mod folder during replacement.

[size=5][color=#42FA60][b]LINKS & SUPPORT[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/northaxosky/fallout4-house-rules][b]GitHub Repository[/b][/url][/*]
[*][url=https://github.com/northaxosky/fallout4-house-rules/issues][b]Issue Tracker[/b][/url][/*]
[*][url=https://github.com/northaxosky/fallout4-house-rules/blob/master/docs/FEATURES.md][b]Setting Reference[/b][/url][/*]
[/list]

Include your game version, F4SE version, chosen menu, and [b]HouseRules.log[/b] when reporting a problem. Describe which setting you changed and what happened.

Logs are saved in: [b]Documents\My Games\Fallout4\F4SE\[/b]
